1
00:05:24,000 --> 00:05:30,000
Where history comes to life.

2
00:10:48,000 --> 00:10:54,000
Night at the Museum is a action, adventure, comedy film directed by Shawn Levy.

3
00:16:12,000 --> 00:16:18,000
Chaos reigns at the natural history museum when night watchman Larry Daley accidentally stirs up an ancient
curse, awakening Attila the Hun, an army of gladiators, a Tyrannosaurus rex and other exhibits.

4
00:21:36,000 --> 00:21:42,000
Larry Daley, played by Ben Stiller.

5
00:27:00,000 --> 00:27:06,000
Rebecca, played by Carla Gugino.

6
00:32:24,000 --> 00:32:30,000
Cecil, played by Dick Van Dyke.

7
00:37:48,000 --> 00:37:54,000
Gus, played by Mickey Rooney.

8
00:43:12,000 --> 00:43:18,000
Reginald, played by Bill Cobbs.

9
00:48:36,000 --> 00:48:42,000
Nick Daley, played by Jake Cherry.

10
00:54:00,000 --> 00:54:06,000
Night at the Museum is a 2006 fantasy comedy film directed by Shawn
Levy and written by Robert Ben Garant and Thomas Lennon.

11
00:59:24,000 --> 00:59:30,000
It is based on the 1993 children's book by Milan Trenc.

12
01:04:48,000 --> 01:04:54,000
The film stars Ben Stiller in the lead role, alongside Carla Gugino, Dick
Van Dyke, Mickey Rooney, Bill Cobbs, and Robin Williams.

13
01:10:12,000 --> 01:10:18,000
It tells the story of a divorced father who applies for a job as a night watchman at New York City's American Museum of Natural
History and subsequently discovers that the exhibits come to life at night, animated by a magical Egyptian artifact.

14
01:15:36,000 --> 01:15:42,000
Night at the Museum premiered in New York City on December 17, 2006, and was
released in the United States on December 22 by 20th Century Fox.

15
01:21:00,000 --> 01:21:06,000
The film received mixed reviews from critics and grossed $574.5
million, becoming the fifth highest-grossing film of 2006.

16
01:26:24,000 --> 01:26:30,000
Two live-action sequels were released: Night at the Museum: Battle of the
Smithsonian in 2009, and Night at the Museum: Secret of the Tomb in 2014.

17
01:31:48,000 --> 01:31:54,000
An animated sequel, Night at the Museum: Kahmunrah Rises
Again, was released in 2022 on Disney+.

18
01:37:12,000 --> 01:37:18,000
The film explores themes of night shift, skeleton,
chaos, maya civilization, museum.

19
01:42:36,000 --> 01:42:42,000
The tone is lighthearted.
